==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc}} {{term|ἐπιδιδυμίς|tr=epididumís|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}, from {{term|ἐπί||upon, over|tr=epi|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}} + {{term|δίδυμος||testicle|sc=Polytonic|tr=didumos|lang=grc}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɛpiˈdɪdɪmɪs/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|pl=[[epididymides]]}}

# {{anatomy}} A narrow, tightly-coiled tube connecting the [[efferent duct]]s from the rear of each [[testicle]] to its [[vas deferens]], where [[sperm]] are stored during maturation.
====Synonym====
*[[paratesticle]]
====Derived terms====
* [[epididymal]]

